."],"report":{"summary":["Credicorp is Peru's largest financial group, with banking, insurance and pension businesses. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 6.4% to S/23.1B in 2025. Net interest income rose 4.3% to S/14.7B and noninterest income rose 10.3% to S/8.4B; noninterest expense rose 8.0%, and the provision for credit losses was S/2.4B, versus S/3.5B.","Net income to Credicorp rose 25.9% to S/6.9B, or S/87.08 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 46.9% versus 46.2%. Credicorp returned S/3.3B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 6.4% to S/23.1B.","Net interest income rose 4.3%.","Noninterest income rose 10.3% to S/8.4B.","Net income to Credicorp rose 25.9% to S/6.9B."],"watch":["Efficiency ratio worsened to 46.9%.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was S/10.8B, up 8.0%.","Credit-loss provision was S/2.4B."],"table":[["Total revenue",23.1061,21.7183,1],["Net interest income",14.7165,14.1151],["Noninterest income",8.3896,7.6031],["Noninterest expense",10.8381,10.0317],["Provision for credit losses",2.4063,3.5194],["Other items, net",0.0858,-0.3426],["Pre-tax income",9.9476,7.8245,1],["Income tax",2.8649,2.2013],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.1573,-0.122],["Net income to Credicorp",6.9254,5.5013,1],["Diluted EPS (S/)",87.08,69.09,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (S/)",483.41438,432.38065,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["Credicorp Ltd. Form 20-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001001290&type=20-F"],["Credicorp financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/bap/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 64% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 64 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"S/23.1B","sub":"revenue · +6.4%","lines":["Net interest income S/14.7B","Noninterest income S/8.4B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 6.4% to S/23.1B.","say":"Revenue rose 6.4%